## T-M10 in LTO links, before LTO's optimizer (ImplementationPlan.md 5.20.3
## T-M10 and 5.20.5 ML2 (1) as amended in section 12; milestone MC-1).
## msil-ld reports
##   'taking the address of the managed-call function '<f>' is not supported for MSIL yet'
## for each use of a managed-call declaration (one with the attribute
## "msil-managed-type") that a bitcode input holds, other than the callee
## of a direct call with the declaration's own function type: each such
## use that the unit's own optimizer left. It reports them before LTO's
## optimizer can internalize a global or fold a use, in full LTO, under
## --lto-partitions, under --lto-emit-asm and as ThinLTO modules (before
## import). After msil-ld's 'error: ', the line names the input that holds
## the use as the link names it ('<input>: ', or '<archive>(<member>): '
## for an archive member), then what holds the use there: 'function @<h>: '
## for a function whose code holds it, and 'global variable @<g>: ' for a
## global variable whose initializer holds it, as slot P0 names such a
## global for clang -c and llc. A function with available_externally
## linkage, a body for inlining only (C99 'inline', GNU 'extern inline'),
## holds none: no output compiles such a body (clang -c's slot P0 still
## meets it at -O0 when always_inline keeps it), and the link keeps
## another unit's definition. Each distinct line comes once per link, so
## each input prints its own lines (in the inputs' order, and for each
## declaration its functions before its globals), and the link writes no
## output. So at one -O level an LTO link refuses what clang -c refuses for
## the same units, except for such a body at -O0.
## The units are the IR that clang -flto -S -emit-llvm writes for
## x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil at -O2 (the *-o0.ll files at -O0), without
## debug information, guids, the summary and the target attributes;
## llvm-as makes full LTO bitcode, and opt -module-summary ThinLTO modules.
## pa.ll, a.ll, b.ll, ac.ll, bc.ll and extaddr.ll are bodies, each linked
## after the head of x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil (win.head) and of
## msil64-unknown-dotnet (net.head) as <unit>-win and <unit>-net (clang
## writes the same bodies for both triples, but for extaddr.ll's char,
## which has neither signext nor zeroext on the Windows triple; the IR
## behaves the same); ea.ll, eb.ll, ya.ll, ya-o2.ll and yb.ll are
## msil64-unknown-dotnet's. f is Contoso.Widget::Guarded(int32) of
## Inputs/fakepack (managed-calls.test) unless an item says otherwise.
## Every link that fails counts its error lines.
## - One unit's global pointer (pa.ll: 'static int f(int v)' with the
##   attribute, 'int (*pa)(int) = &f;' and 'int main(void) { return
##   pa(-3); }'): one line, for pa.ll's input and global variable @pa, in
##   full LTO, as a ThinLTO module, under --lto-partitions=2 and under
##   --lto-emit-asm, on each triple, as clang -c gives it. These links used
##   to succeed: LTO internalized pa and turned main's call through it into
##   a direct call before slot P0 ran.
## - Two units, each with its own static f (a.ll: 'int (*pa)(int) = &f;';
##   b.ll: 'extern int (*pa)(int); int main(void) { return pa == &f ? 1 :
##   2; }'). In C the two f's are two functions, so main must return 2, but
##   both units name f '__msil_mc.f.__uniq.<n>' with one <n> (the
##   declarations would make equal stubs), so LTO took them for one
##   function. The link fails with two lines, a.ll's input's for global
##   variable @pa and b.ll's input's for function @main, each once (sorted,
##   as their order follows the inputs), in full LTO and as ThinLTO modules
##   in both input orders, under --lto-partitions=2 and under
##   --lto-emit-asm, on each triple, and at -O0 (a-o0.ll and b-o0.ll) in
##   full LTO and as ThinLTO modules. Each of those links used to succeed
##   with a main that returns 1.
## - The same two units, each with a function that nothing calls, which
##   calls f through a cast pointer (ac.ll: 'long long unusedA(void) {
##   return ((long long (*)(long long))f)(1); }'; bc.ll: unusedB, the
##   same): a direct call with another function type, which slot P0 refuses
##   with T-M17 for clang -c,
##   'managed call '<f>' is declared with different 'msil_method' or 'msil_catch' arguments in different translation units'.
##   msil-ld reports T-M17 before LTO, once per name, for a declaration of
##   a bitcode input that its own unit calls with another function type, or
##   with a signext or zeroext of its own that would change the
##   declaration's stub (the calls in available_externally functions
##   aside), and gives that declaration no T-M10 line: the pair fails with
##   the T-M17 line alone in full LTO, as ThinLTO modules, under
##   --lto-partitions=2 and under --lto-emit-asm, on each triple. These
##   links used to succeed with a main that returns 1: msil-ld left the
##   declarations to slot P0, and LTO's optimizer deleted unusedA and
##   unusedB with their calls and folded main's comparison. Beside the
##   other unit without its cast call (ac.ll with b.ll, a.ll with bc.ll),
##   each unit gets its own line, as clang -c gives them: T-M17 for the
##   unit with the cast call, T-M10 for the other one's holder. ea.ll and eb.ll
##   are the pair as 'static short f(short v)', bound to System.Math::Abs
##   'int16(int16)' (these links stop before binding), each with a function
##   that nothing calls, which calls f through '(unsigned short
##   (*)(short))f', a zeroext result of its own against the declaration's
##   signext: the T-M17 line alone, in full LTO, as ThinLTO modules and
##   under --lto-emit-asm; they used to link. deadcast.ll is one unit with
##   such a call to another function type in a function that nothing calls
##   ('long long unusedA(void) { return ((long long (*)(long long))f)(1);
##   }'), a direct call in main ('int main(void) { return f(-3); }') and no
##   address: the T-M17 line alone in full LTO, as a ThinLTO module and
##   under --lto-emit-asm, as clang -c gives it; it used to link.
## - A static pointer that the unit's own optimizer folds into a direct
##   call (sp.ll: 'static int (*sp)(int) = &f;' and 'int main(void) {
##   return sp(-3); }', where main calls f directly) links in full LTO and
##   as a ThinLTO module, and main calls the stub, which calls Guarded. At
##   -O0 (sp-o0.ll, which keeps sp) the unit fails with one line, for
##   sp-o0.ll's input and global variable @sp, in both, as clang -c -O0
##   does; it used to link.
## - An address in a branch that the unit's own optimizer deletes, f
##   external: s1.ll's 'int g(int x) { return f(x); }', s2.ll's 'static long
##   long h(int y) { return y ? (long long)(__INTPTR_TYPE__)&f : 0; }' and
##   'int k(int x) { return (int)h(0) + 0 * x; }', and sm.ll's 'int
##   main(void) { return 100 + g(-3) * 10 + k(-4); }'. At -O2 s2.ll's k
##   returns 0 and no use of f is left, and the units link in full LTO and
##   as ThinLTO modules. At -O0 (s1-o0.ll, s2-o0.ll and sm-o0.ll) h keeps
##   the address, and the units fail with one line, for s2-o0.ll's input and
##   function @h, in full LTO, as ThinLTO modules, under --lto-partitions=2,
##   under --lto-emit-asm, and in a mixed link of s2-o0.ll's bitcode with
##   llc's objects of s1-o0.ll and sm-o0.ll. Those links used to stop with
##   slot P0's line from LTO's code generation,
##   'msil-ld: error: <unknown>:0:0: in function h i64 (i32): taking the address ...'.
## - a.ll's bitcode beside llc's object of pm.ll ('extern int (*pa)(int);
##   int main(void) { return pa(-3); }') fails with a.ll's input's line,
##   once.
## - Two inputs whose holders have one name, f external, at -O0 (ha.ll and
##   hb.ll: 'static void hold(void) { reg(&f); }', with 'void a_init(void)
##   { hold(); }' and b_init; hm.ll: 'void reg(int (*cb)(int)) { saved =
##   cb; }' and a main that calls a_init and b_init): two lines, function
##   @hold for each input, in full LTO, as ThinLTO modules and under
##   --lto-partitions=2, in the inputs' order when they are not sorted. ga.ll
##   and gb.ll ('static int (*sp)(int) = &f;', with a_use and b_use, which
##   call sp, and gm.ll's main, which calls both): two lines, global
##   variable @sp for each input, in full LTO and as ThinLTO modules. ha.ll's
##   bitcode as a member of libha.a gives 'libha.a(ha.bc): function @hold:
##   ...'. These links used to print one line, which named no input.
## - A use in an available_externally function: xa.ll's 'extern inline
##   __attribute__((gnu_inline)) int g(int x) { if (x == 12345) keep(f);
##   return x; }' and its '__attribute__((optnone, noinline)) int use(int
##   x) { return g(x) + f(x); }', whose -flto IR keeps g's body for
##   inlining; xb.ll defines g, keep and main. The pair links without a
##   diagnostic in full LTO, as ThinLTO modules and as xa.ll's bitcode with
##   llc's object of xb.ll, as llc's objects of xa-o2.ll (xa.ll's unit at
##   -O2 without -flto, where clang dropped g's body, as clang -c compiles
##   it) and xb.ll do, and in each image use calls g, xb.ll's.
##   ya.ll, ya-o2.ll and yb.ll are the same units with a
##   C99 inline definition ('inline int g(int x)') on msil64-unknown-dotnet,
##   and link the same way. Those LTO links used to fail with T-M10 for
##   function @g. When the definition that the link keeps takes the address
##   itself (xc.ll's external g, whose noinline keep stores the pointer),
##   xc.ll's input gets its line, once, in full LTO and as ThinLTO modules.
##   A call with another function type there gets no T-M17 either: xd.ll's
##   GNU inline g calls f only through a cast pointer ('return (int)((long
##   long (*)(long long))f)(x);'), and xd.ll with xb.ll links without a
##   diagnostic in full LTO, as ThinLTO modules and as xd.ll's bitcode with
##   llc's object of xb.ll.
## - A declaration that T-M17 refuses gets no T-M10 line. t17a.ll binds an
##   external f to Guarded and takes its address ('int (*keep)(int) =
##   &f;'), and t17b.ll binds f to Contoso.Point::Twice(int32) and calls it:
##   T-M17 alone, before LTO, in full LTO, as ThinLTO modules and under
##   --lto-emit-asm. castaddr.ll calls an external f through a cast to 'long
##   long (*)(long long)' and takes its address ('int (*keep)(int) = &f;'):
##   msil-ld's T-M17 for that call, before LTO, is the link's one line in
##   those modes, as slot P0's is clang -c's one line. extaddr.ll binds f to
##   Contoso.Widget::Octet(uint8) as 'unsigned char f(unsigned char)', takes
##   its address ('unsigned char (*keep)(unsigned char) = &f;') and calls it
##   through '(signed char (*)(unsigned char))f', a signext result of its
##   own that would end the stub in conv.i1 where the declaration's zeroext
##   ends it in conv.u1: the T-M17 line alone, in full LTO, as a ThinLTO
##   module and under --lto-emit-asm, on each triple, and no output.

# REQUIRES: llvm-cil-dump
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: mkdir refs
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeRuntime.yaml -o refs/FakeRuntime.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeWidgets.yaml -o refs/FakeWidgets.dll
# DEFINE: %{crash} = --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR"
# DEFINE: %{err} = FileCheck %s %{crash} --implicit-check-not=error: --implicit-check-not=warning:
## A failed link's error lines (err.txt), counted, then each pinned whole;
## two lines are sorted first.
# DEFINE: %{one} = grep error: err.txt | count 1 && %{err} --input-file=err.txt
# DEFINE: %{two} = grep error: err.txt | count 2 && sort err.txt | %{err}

## Each T-M10 line names its input: IN, or A and B (A's line sorts first).
# TM10-PA:   {{^}}msil-ld: error: [[IN]]: global variable @pa: taking the address of the managed-call function 'f' is not supported for MSIL yet{{$}}
# TM10-PAIR: {{^}}msil-ld: error: [[A]]: global variable @pa: taking the address of the managed-call function 'f' is not supported for MSIL yet{{$}}
# TM10-PAIR: {{^}}msil-ld: error: [[B]]: function @main: taking the address of the managed-call function 'f' is not supported for MSIL yet{{$}}
# TM10-MAIN: {{^}}msil-ld: error: [[IN]]: function @main: taking the address of the managed-call function 'f' is not supported for MSIL yet{{$}}
# TM10-SP:   {{^}}msil-ld: error: [[IN]]: global variable @sp: taking the address of the managed-call function 'f' is not supported for MSIL yet{{$}}
# TM10-H:    {{^}}msil-ld: error: [[IN]]: function @h: taking the address of the managed-call function 'f' is not supported for MSIL yet{{$}}
# TM10-HOLD: {{^}}msil-ld: error: [[A]]: function @hold: taking the address of the managed-call function 'f' is not supported for MSIL yet{{$}}
# TM10-HOLD: {{^}}msil-ld: error: [[B]]: function @hold: taking the address of the managed-call function 'f' is not supported for MSIL yet{{$}}
# TM10-SPS:  {{^}}msil-ld: error: [[A]]: global variable @sp: taking the address of the managed-call function 'f' is not supported for MSIL yet{{$}}
# TM10-SPS:  {{^}}msil-ld: error: [[B]]: global variable @sp: taking the address of the managed-call function 'f' is not supported for MSIL yet{{$}}
# TM10-G:    {{^}}msil-ld: error: [[IN]]: function @g: taking the address of the managed-call function 'f' is not supported for MSIL yet{{$}}
# TM17:      {{^}}msil-ld: error: managed call 'f' is declared with different 'msil_method' or 'msil_catch' arguments in different translation units{{$}}

## The units of both triples: on the triple %{tr}, each body after the
## triple's head (<unit>-%{tr}.ll), as full LTO bitcode and as a ThinLTO
## module.
# DEFINE: %{tr} =
# DEFINE: %{units} = \
# DEFINE:   cat %{tr}.head pa.ll > pa-%{tr}.ll && cat %{tr}.head a.ll > a-%{tr}.ll && \
# DEFINE:   cat %{tr}.head b.ll > b-%{tr}.ll && cat %{tr}.head ac.ll > ac-%{tr}.ll && \
# DEFINE:   cat %{tr}.head bc.ll > bc-%{tr}.ll && cat %{tr}.head extaddr.ll > extaddr-%{tr}.ll && \
# DEFINE:   llvm-as pa-%{tr}.ll -o pa-%{tr}.bc && opt -module-summary pa-%{tr}.ll -o pa-%{tr}.thin.bc && \
# DEFINE:   llvm-as a-%{tr}.ll -o a-%{tr}.bc && opt -module-summary a-%{tr}.ll -o a-%{tr}.thin.bc && \
# DEFINE:   llvm-as b-%{tr}.ll -o b-%{tr}.bc && opt -module-summary b-%{tr}.ll -o b-%{tr}.thin.bc && \
# DEFINE:   llvm-as ac-%{tr}.ll -o ac-%{tr}.bc && opt -module-summary ac-%{tr}.ll -o ac-%{tr}.thin.bc && \
# DEFINE:   llvm-as bc-%{tr}.ll -o bc-%{tr}.bc && opt -module-summary bc-%{tr}.ll -o bc-%{tr}.thin.bc && \
# DEFINE:   llvm-as extaddr-%{tr}.ll -o extaddr-%{tr}.bc && \
# DEFINE:   opt -module-summary extaddr-%{tr}.ll -o extaddr-%{tr}.thin.bc
## One unit's global pointer: one line in every LTO mode, and no output.
# DEFINE: %{pa} = \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld pa-%{tr}.bc --reference=refs -o x.exe 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{one} --check-prefix=TM10-PA -DIN=pa-%{tr}.bc && \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld pa-%{tr}.thin.bc --reference=refs -o x.exe 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{one} --check-prefix=TM10-PA -DIN=pa-%{tr}.thin.bc && \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld pa-%{tr}.bc --lto-partitions=2 --reference=refs -o x.exe 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{one} --check-prefix=TM10-PA -DIN=pa-%{tr}.bc && \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld --lto-emit-asm pa-%{tr}.bc -o x.il 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{one} --check-prefix=TM10-PA -DIN=pa-%{tr}.bc && \
# DEFINE:   not ls x.exe && not ls x.il
## Two units' static f: two lines, each once, in every LTO mode and order.
# DEFINE: %{pair} = \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld a-%{tr}.bc b-%{tr}.bc --reference=refs -o x.exe 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{two} --check-prefix=TM10-PAIR -DA=a-%{tr}.bc -DB=b-%{tr}.bc && \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld b-%{tr}.bc a-%{tr}.bc --reference=refs -o x.exe 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{two} --check-prefix=TM10-PAIR -DA=a-%{tr}.bc -DB=b-%{tr}.bc && \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld a-%{tr}.thin.bc b-%{tr}.thin.bc --reference=refs -o x.exe 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{two} --check-prefix=TM10-PAIR -DA=a-%{tr}.thin.bc -DB=b-%{tr}.thin.bc && \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld b-%{tr}.thin.bc a-%{tr}.thin.bc --reference=refs -o x.exe 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{two} --check-prefix=TM10-PAIR -DA=a-%{tr}.thin.bc -DB=b-%{tr}.thin.bc && \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld a-%{tr}.bc b-%{tr}.bc --lto-partitions=2 --reference=refs -o x.exe 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{two} --check-prefix=TM10-PAIR -DA=a-%{tr}.bc -DB=b-%{tr}.bc && \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld --lto-emit-asm a-%{tr}.bc b-%{tr}.bc -o x.il 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{two} --check-prefix=TM10-PAIR -DA=a-%{tr}.bc -DB=b-%{tr}.bc && \
# DEFINE:   not ls x.exe && not ls x.il
## The same units with their calls through a cast pointer: T-M17 alone,
## before LTO, in every LTO mode, and no output; beside a unit without it,
## each unit's own line (sorted: the T-M10 line first).
# DEFINE: %{cast} = \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld ac-%{tr}.bc bc-%{tr}.bc --reference=refs -o x.exe 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{one} --check-prefix=TM17 && \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld ac-%{tr}.thin.bc bc-%{tr}.thin.bc --reference=refs -o x.exe 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{one} --check-prefix=TM17 && \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld ac-%{tr}.bc bc-%{tr}.bc --lto-partitions=2 --reference=refs -o x.exe 2> err.txt && \
# DEFINE:     %{one} --check-prefix=TM17 && \
# DEFINE:   not msil-ld --lto-emit-asm ac-%{tr}.bc bc-%{tr}.bc -o x.il 2> err.txt && \
